body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When `renderMissing` is `false` (which is the default behavior), `ensureRenderFiles` checks if the render files exist on disk but does not record any critical diagnostics if they are missing. This allows the script to proceed to the VLM execution phase, where `imagePathToDataUrl` will attempt to read the missing files and throw a raw `ENOENT` file system error.

To fail-closed gracefully and prevent unnecessary/failed external API calls, we should record a critical diagnostic if any required render file is missing when `renderMissing` is `false`.

```javascript
  if (!renderMissing) {
    for (const packet of packets) {
      for (const render of asArray(packet.source_page_renders)) {
        const exists = fs.existsSync(resolvePath(root, render.output_path));
        if (!exists) {
          diagnostics.push({
            code: 'source_page_render_missing',
            severity: 'critical',
            packet_id: packet.packet_id,
            source_page_render_id: render.source_page_render_id,
            output_path: render.output_path,
            reason: 'Render file does not exist on disk',
          });
        }
        receipts.push({
          packet_id: packet.packet_id,
          source_page_render_id: render.source_page_render_id,
          output_path: render.output_path,
          exists,
          sha256: exists ? sha256File(root, render.output_path) : null,
          rendered_during_run: false,
        });
      }
    }
    return receipts;
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Ensure validation and check scripts handle missing or malformed critical artifacts gracefully without throwing unhandled exceptions. They should fail-closed by returning a failed validation status, a failure count, and diagnostic codes, backed by regression tests.
2. When generating artifact receipts, check if the file exists before attempting to calculate its hash (e.g., SHA-256) to prevent raw file system errors (like ENOENT) from crashing the script when optional files are missing. If the file is missing, record the hash as null and preserve the existence metadata.
</details>

